{"ts":1793397764964,"event":"done","summary":"PLAT-103 shipped. validateApp now throws when owner is missing or empty; contracts released as 2.0.0 (breaking, major bump; CD published it). Billing (owner 'payments'), core shell ('platform') and reports ('insights') pass owner from package.json 'team', bump @mfe/shared-contracts to ^2.0.0 with lockfiles, and are deployed. PRs: contracts #1, billing #2, shell #3, reports #4 (all CI green, CD green). Assumptions: (1) reports also calls validateApp, so I added it as an extra sub-task though the ticket did not list it; (2) owner values are hardcoded to the package.json team rather than read at runtime; (3) 'missing or empty' means falsy, so whitespace-only owners are accepted; (4) the first contracts PR was opened before its commit existed, so I pushed the commit to the same PR with st pr push."}
